block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Estimate the false-positive blast radius by auditing existing cross-artifact byte/text-equality tests the new rule would fire on, and specify how a legitimately-comparing (timestamp-free) test escapes the gate given no suppression marker and no clock to freeze.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Out of Scope: 'Parsing product code to prove whether a compared artifact embeds timestamps.'","Out of Scope: 'Adding a new configuration mechanism or suppression marker beyond the existing checker patterns.'","Escape is keyed only on 'monkeypatch.setattr(..., \"_now_iso\", ...)' / '\"utc_now_iso\"'","AC: 'followed before push by make verify' — the new rule will run against the whole tests/** corpus","ABSENCE: the plan's Out of Scope defers 'Auditing all existing cross-artifact byte-equality tests beyond what the checker and its test suite exercise', so the blast radius on the live tree is unmeasured"],"finding":"The rule fires on every cross-artifact read_bytes()/read_text() equality comparison regardless of whether the artifact actually embeds a timestamp, but the only escape is freezing _now_iso/utc_now_iso — which is unavailable for tests comparing timestamp-free artifacts — and a new suppression marker is explicitly out of scope. The plan does not estimate this false-positive surface, yet the lint runs in make verify.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3a4016e01cb74aff","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope / Out of Scope / Decision","norm_id":"n243e09c695584eb3","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A test asserts fileA.read_bytes() == golden.read_bytes() where the artifact has no timestamp; the new rule fires, but the author cannot freeze a clock (there is none) and has no suppression marker, forcing a rewrite to satisfy the gate","make verify newly fails on pre-